course: dictionary
lesson: 4409
title: One word, many places: hall
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the clues around it show you which one the writer means. The word hall is a good example. «Shout hello in a big empty hall and a moment later the walls shout it back.» Big, empty and echoing tells you this hall is a large room.
explain: Now look at «Badger's great secret: there is an underground passage from the river-bank right up into the middle of Toad Hall.» Toad Hall is the name of a house, so hall here means a home or building. Check by swapping in your meaning: "the middle of Toad House" still makes sense.
explain: A hall can also be the passage inside a house, the space by the front door. Always ask: what clue is in the sentence? A big room with a crowd, or a passage with doors? Your clue points to the right meaning.
fact: A hall is a big room for meetings, concerts, plays or school assemblies.
fact: A hallway, or hall, is a passage inside a building, or the space by the front door of a house.
fact: Some big buildings are called halls, like a town hall or a hall of residence.
fact: A Hall of Fame is a place that honours famous people.
fact: In old stories, «Odysseus» came home to his hall, a great room where men were feasting, so hall can also mean a grand room for feasts.
exercise: «Shout hello in a big empty hall and a moment later the walls shout it back.» What is a hall in this sentence? | A type of bird | A tiny garden shed | *A big room | A pen for animals
exercise: «There is an underground passage right up into the middle of Toad Hall.» In this sentence, what does Toad Hall name? | A school | *A house or home | A kind of meal | A bridge over the river
exercise: Ella says a hall can only be a corridor. What is a sports hall? | A kind of wooden fence | A long passage by the door | A type of lunch | *A room with a big floor for sport
test: Which kind of hall would you use for a school play? | A space under the stairs | A corridor in the sports centre | *The school hall | A hallway by the front door
test: Which phrase names a place that honours famous people? | *Hall of Fame | Down the hall | Hall pass | Town hall
exam: Which sentence uses hall to mean a passage inside a building? | We sat in the school hall for assembly | The Hall of Fame honours stars | The town hall is opposite the park | *Please walk, do not run, down the hall
